  "summary": "Seven preprints probe optimizer, measurement-cost, and input-encoding choices in variational and reservoir quantum learning, with several reporting classical parity.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is how parameterized and fixed-dynamics quantum models are trained and read out. On the variational side, a Krotov-inspired discrete adjoint optimizer with a hybrid online-to-batch schedule, frozen LLMs proposing circuit parameters (effective for structured Hamiltonians, worse than Adam on random ones), and a learned controller cutting VQE gradient shots by 49.6% target optimization and measurement cost. On the reservoir side, data re-uploading improves higher-order nonlinear processing and chaotic-series tasks, while multi-layer quantum extreme learning machines with MMD-fitted linear readouts match a classical random-feature baseline. Benchmarks of variational quantum recurrent networks quantify memory and nonlinear capacity against classical baselines, and quantum RL work ablates architecture search and non-local observables. Several results indicate parity rather than advantage.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
